From 2008c1ec4c75c43db34d85adc32da226c2c6d9f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:50:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] Eden (Doris): undo build 17's extra texture-removal
 cancelling; report cache lock waits, copies of GPU-written bytes and
 wait-for-idle details

- Build 17 also called off a pending texture removal whenever another texture over the same
  memory was created, removed or drawn into. In TotK that loop started 1850 copies back every
  10 seconds (build 16: 156) and called most of them off again. Back to build 16's rules (sparse
  textures still skipped, pressure threshold stays 2.45 GiB).
- Report: GPU thread time waiting for the texture/buffer cache locks in draws, how long fence
  handling holds them, how often the game wrote to pages with GPU-written bytes (Eden
  #4490/#4531 copy those back first) and how long it waited; how many wait-for-idles came
  inside a render pass and how many had no storage writes by draws before them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
